WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.599
Each test I D routes to a finding family,

2
00:00:02.599 --> 00:00:06.662
and each family to the page in
the workbook that remediates it.

3
00:00:06.662 --> 00:00:09.139
The table is from Close Before You Assess,

4
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.437
with the evidence the guide adds for
when a finding is ready for closure.

5
00:00:13.437 --> 00:00:16.650
Emergency access goes to
Access and Privilege,

6
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.438
and is ready when the sign-in
alert fired on a test sign-in.

7
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:24.242
Standing privilege goes to its
PIM chapter, and is ready when no

8
00:00:24.242 --> 00:00:28.338
permanent active assignment sits
outside the exception register.

9
00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:31.656
Device compliance goes to
Devices and Endpoints,

10
00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:34.975
ready when a noncompliant
test device is refused.

11
00:00:34.975 --> 00:00:38.913
Application secrets go to
Governance, Drift and Evidence.

12
00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:41.688
DDoS and web application firewall findings

13
00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:44.388
go to the Azure Security
Engineering guide.

14
00:00:44.388 --> 00:00:49.413
A finding no family covers is unrouted,
and goes to the Zero Trust program lead.

15
00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:53.558
In release three point one point
oh, the email and collaboration

16
00:00:53.558 --> 00:00:58.630
threat-protection tests have no family
yet, so they stay unrouted and visible.
